# Jenkins Build Triggers

Jenkins supports different mechanisms for triggering Jobs.

## Build Periodically

Reference:

[Crontab Guru](https://crontab.guru/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

* Triggers Jenkins Jobs according to a cron schedule.
* Does not depend on source-code changes.
* Useful for scheduled process automation.
* Not specifically intended for CI/CD source-code change detection.

Example:

```text
Jenkins_Start_Jobs
    ↓
Start Servers
    ↓
Scheduled: 7:45 AM

Jenkins_Stop_Jobs
    ↓
Stop Servers
    ↓
Scheduled: 10:15 PM
```

## GitHub Webhook

* Used for CI/CD.
* Triggers a Jenkins Job when a commit/change occurs in the remote GitHub repository.
* The GitHub repository must be configured with the Jenkins webhook URL.

Example:

```text
GitHub Repository
      |
      | Commit
      ↓
GitHub Webhook
      |
      ↓
Jenkins
      |
      ↓
CI/CD Pipeline
```

## Poll SCM

* Checks the source-code repository based on a cron schedule.
* Triggers the build only when changes are detected.

Example use case:

```text
QA Testing Team
    ↓
Testing Cycles
    ├── 8 AM
    ├── 12 PM
    └── 3 PM
```

---

# Jenkins Email Notifications

Email notifications can be configured for events such as:

* Successful execution.
* Failure.
* Aborted execution.

## Gmail SMTP Configuration

Before configuring Jenkins email notifications:

1. Enable Two-Factor Authentication/MFA on the Gmail account.
2. Create a Gmail App Password.
3. Configure the SMTP server in Jenkins.

### Jenkins SMTP Configuration

```text
SMTP Server:
smtp.gmail.com

SMTP Port:
465

SSL:
Enabled

Authentication:
Enabled

Username:
Gmail Account

Password:
Gmail App Password
```

> Never store or share the actual Gmail App Password in notes, source code, or pipeline scripts.

## Example Email Notification

```groovy
post {
    failure {
        mail(
            body: "Jenkins Job Status: ${BUILD_URL}",
            subject: "Build Failed - ${JOB_NAME} (${BUILD_NUMBER})",
            to: "recipient@example.com"
        )
    }

    success {
        mail(
            body: "Jenkins Job Status: ${BUILD_URL}",
            subject: "Build Successful - ${JOB_NAME} (${BUILD_NUMBER})",
            to: "recipient@example.com"
        )
    }

    aborted {
        mail(
            body: "Jenkins Job Status: ${BUILD_URL}",
            subject: "Build Aborted - ${JOB_NAME} (${BUILD_NUMBER})",
            to: "recipient@example.com"
        )
    }
}
```

